.TH SIG_UNSHIELD 3 "15 Mar 2023" "CB" "Library Functions"

.SH NAME
sig_unshield \- Unblock a set of signals

.SH SYNOPSIS
.IB #include <lib/sig.h>

.IB int
.IB sig_unshield(void);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBsig_unshield\fR function is used to unblock a set of signals. It takes no arguments.

.SH RETURN VALUE
The \fBsig_unshield\fR function returns 0 on success, and -1 on failure.

.SH EXAMPLES
The following example demonstrates how to use the \fBsig_unshield\fR function:

.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/sig.h>

int main() {
    printf("Unshielding signals...\n");

    int r = sig_unshield();

    if(r == 0)
        printf("Signals unshielded successfully.\n");
    else
        printf("Failed to unshield signals.\n");

    return 0;
}
.nef